    [Doc][Model] Add GLM-5.3 PP PD and MemCache pooling deployment guide (#18168)
    
    ### What this PR does / why we need it?
    
    Adds GLM-5.3 W8A8C8 A3 deployment instructions for the supplied 198K
    workload, with a 200,000-token maximum model length, both without
    pooling and with MemCache KV pooling. Prefill uses DP1/TP16/PP2 over
    P0/P1 with a 42/36 layer partition; Decode uses DP16/TP2 over D0/D1. The
    guide includes separate complete P0, P1, D0, and D1 scripts and per-node
    startup commands for both deployment modes, a Decode DP launcher, all 17
    proxy endpoints, and cache-reuse verification.
    
    Continues #17841 by aisong1988. All eight original commits are
    cherry-picked with their author, sign-off, and source commit references
    preserved. The original environment/version separation, MemCache
    prerequisites, and verification guidance are retained and adapted to the
    supplied PP configurations. The layout and deployment/verification
    approach follow #17773.
    
    The new scripts use MooncakeConnectorV2 and retain the supplied batch
    budgets, MTP settings, int8 KV/indexer cache, async scheduling, and
    pooling settings. Reusable installation paths, P1's shared master and
    headless node rank, and distinct per-engine IDs make the multi-node
    instructions complete. Ascend Store's lookup identifier remains "0"
    because its IPC path includes the DP rank.
    
    All GLM-5.3 serving examples and the FAQ now explicitly use the `glm47`
    reasoning parser, including the existing A3/A2 co-located examples.
    
    ### Does this PR introduce _any_ user-facing change?
    
    Documentation only. No runtime code changes. The existing co-located
    examples remain available, with their v0.23.0 requirements separated
    from the 0.30.0RC PD reference.
    
    ### How was this patch tested?
    
    - Full MkDocs build passed; the generated HTML preserves all new
    copyable Python and shell blocks exactly.
    - Markdownlint with the repository-pinned v0.45.0, codespell with
    repository settings, typos v1.32.0, and `git diff --check` passed.
    - All 26 shell blocks passed `bash -n`; the Python launcher parsed
    successfully.
    - Executed mocked shell commands for 36 role/rank cases (P0/P1 and all
    16 Decode ranks in each mode). Checked PP master/rank, P1 headless mode,
    API ports, TP/DP sizes, model length, and sequence/batch budgets. All
    supplied JSON settings are identical except for the intentionally
    distinct engine IDs.
    - Checked launcher device assignments and arguments for all 16 Decode
    ranks, proxy host/port mappings for all 17 endpoints, and relative file
    links. Also passed each of the four documented Decode startup commands
    through the actual launcher argument parser and mocked process entry
    point, verifying all 32 generated rank launches, script selections, and
    the seven positional arguments. Confirmed all 12 serving commands use
    glm47 and all node scripts precede the grouped startup commands.
    - Attempted the required full-repository `bash format.sh ci`; it stalled
    while installing the actionlint environment and was stopped. Relevant
    document checks were run separately; full-repository lint remains for
    CI.
    - NPU deployment, inference, and performance have not been run by this
    agent. The GPQA Diamond PD-disaggregation accuracy results were supplied
    by the contributor: A3 91.92 and A2 89.39; the old v0.23.0 accuracy
    description and results were replaced.
    
    Target branch: `main`.
    
